{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the sense of <b>and the people sat down to eat and drink</b> is that all of them sat together as one to eat to satiety and drink to drunkenness, as is done on festivals and appointed times, and afterward they rose to make sport with their idols and for rejoicing. And Scripture recounts this on account of what He said, <b>\"the sound of singing I hear\"</b> (Exodus 32:18), for Moses found them making sport before him, and his heart was uplifted in the ways of HaShem to take it from before them and burn it before their eyes, and he made them drink it. And the verse completed all that they did with the calf, and afterward it recounted what HaShem said to Moses, <b>\"Go, get you down\"</b> — but this utterance to Moses was in the early morning when they bowed down to it and sacrificed to it, and when Moses came down they sat to eat and drink and rose to make sport, and he found them in the sport. And this too is proof for what I explained (Ramban on Exodus 32:1), that it was not said to Moses, \"go, get you down, for your people has corrupted itself,\" on the day that Aaron made the calf and the altar — for he would have come down immediately — but when the people sacrificed and bowed down to it, then He said to Moses that he should go down."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:19:55.511655907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}